# tests/container.def -- container platform definition template for rt.sh
# (see tests/stampede.def for a filled-in example for Stampede3)
#
# Usage:
#   1. Edit the values at the end of this file for your own platform (keep a
#      copy of the original as a reference).
#   2. Run:
#        ./rt.sh -a <account> -P container.def [-l rt.conf] [-s my_test.list]
#
#      -l rt.conf       file with the list of tests (rt.conf is the default);
#                       can also be your own file, e.g. -l my_rt.conf
#      -s my_test.list  optional: run only the tests listed in my_test.list,
#                       one "<test name> <compiler>" per line, for example:
#                         control_c48 oneapi
#                         control_p8 oneapi
#
# Tests are selected from rt.conf (or -l <file>) with the machine name
# "container" in the Machines column, like any other machine:
# "+ ... container" runs a line in the container, "- ... container"
# excludes it, and an empty column runs it everywhere.
#
# This file is a bash file of KEY=value assignments, sourced by rt.sh.
# Quote values containing spaces. By default a container run is sequential
# and skips baseline comparison: a portability check ("does the model build
# and run here at all?"), not a regression test. -c/-m opt into baseline
# creation/comparison; -r/-e opt into Rocoto/ecFlow (needs ROCOTO_SCHEDULER
# and/or WORKFLOW_MODULE_CMD). See the User's Guide chapter "Container
# Option to Test and Run the UFS Weather Model" for the full field reference.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Platform and container
#
#   PLATFORM_NAME  Required. Must be "container". Becomes MACHINE_ID for
#                  this run: the machine name matched in rt.conf, and the
#                  suffix of the *_container job-card templates and
#                  modulefiles.
#   CONTAINER_IMG_ONEAPI Absolute path to an Intel oneAPI Singularity/Apptainer
#                        image (*.sif) on this host.
#   CONTAINER_IMG_GNU    Absolute path to a GNU Singularity/Apptainer image
#                        (*.sif) on this host.
#                        At least one image is required; rt.sh stops with an
#                        error if neither is set, or if a path that is set
#                        does not exist. Each rt.conf line uses the image for
#                        its compiler. Lines for a compiler with no image are
#                        skipped with a notice, not an error.
#   BIND_DIRS            Comma-separated host directories to bind-mount into
#                        the container (must cover the source tree, input
#                        data, and RUNDIR_ROOT).
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scheduler
#
#   TPN         Required. Tasks-Per-Node: MPI tasks per node on this
#               platform, a numeric entry (e.g., 48 on Stampede3).
#   SCHEDULER   Required. "slurm", "pbs", or "none" for an
#               interactive/no-scheduler run.
#   PARTITION   Slurm partition name (blank for PBS or no scheduler).
#   QUEUE       Slurm QOS / PBS queue name (blank for no scheduler).
#   MPI_LAUNCH_ONEAPI  MPI launch command for Intel oneAPI tests, used when SCHEDULER
#                     is "none" and in PBS job cards (defaults to "mpiexec"
#                     if blank).
#   MPI_LAUNCH_GNU    The same for GNU tests (defaults to "mpirun" if blank).
#
#   The scheduler account/project is set only with rt.sh's own -a <account>
#   on the command line.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Run directory
#
#   RUNDIR_ROOT  Required. Top-level directory where compile and test run
#                directories are created. Should be a user-writable path,
#                preferably on a scratch or work filesystem.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Input data
#
#   INPUTDATA_ROOT       Required. Staged input-data directory (fix files
#                        and other RT input data).
#   INPUTDATA_ROOT_WW3   Optional. Defaults to a WW3_input_data_* sibling
#                        directory under INPUTDATA_ROOT if left blank.
#   INPUTDATA_LM4        Optional. Defaults to an LM4_input_data
#                        subdirectory of INPUTDATA_ROOT if left blank.
#   INPUTDATA_GFSv17opn  Optional. Only needed by tests that explicitly
#                        require GFSv17 operational input data.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Workflow manager (optional; only needed to use -r or -e)
#
#   ROCOTO_SCHEDULER    Rocoto's own scheduler-driver name -- not always the
#                       same as SCHEDULER (e.g. plain PBS is "pbs" but
#                       PBS Professional is "pbspro"). Required to use -r.
#                       Example: ROCOTO_SCHEDULER=slurm
#   WORKFLOW_MODULE_CMD A shell command run to put rocoto's or ecflow's
#                       command-line tools on PATH. Leave blank if already
#                       on PATH.
#                       Example: WORKFLOW_MODULE_CMD='module load rocoto/1.3.7'
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------

PLATFORM_NAME=container
CONTAINER_IMG_ONEAPI=/path/to/containers/rocky9-oneapi2024.2-ss192.sif
CONTAINER_IMG_GNU=/path/to/containers/rocky9-gcc13-ss192-ompi416.sif
BIND_DIRS='/path1,/path2,/path3'

TPN=192
SCHEDULER=slurm
PARTITION=mypartition
QUEUE=myqueue
MPI_LAUNCH_ONEAPI=mpiexec
MPI_LAUNCH_GNU=mpirun

RUNDIR_ROOT=/path/to/runtime_dir

INPUTDATA_ROOT=/path/to/input-data
INPUTDATA_ROOT_WW3=
INPUTDATA_LM4=
INPUTDATA_GFSv17opn=

ROCOTO_SCHEDULER=
WORKFLOW_MODULE_CMD=
